launch terminal.app

type:
touch ~/.nethackrc

[creates an empty file called .nethackrc at the top of your user 
directory]

then either edit it in vi or your text-editor of choice (e.g. 
BBEdit Lite using "Open hidden...")

For the Qt settings use:
qt_tilewidth=13
qt_tileheight=23
qt_fontsize=large
qt_compact=0

[with values that suit you, these are mine, fits 1056*792 nicely]

rather than the usual:
OPTIONS=key:value

[Put another way: treat the OS X version as a unix version, because 
it is.]

Also, it would probably be a good idea to use:
OPTIONS=name:player

in there somewhere.

